# Icons — do not invent or generate

Inline UI icons are defined in:

- [`app/utils/icons-template.js`](app/utils/icons-template.js) — template catalogue (`TEMPLATE_ICONS`; synced / hashed)
- [`app/utils/icons-app.js`](app/utils/icons-app.js) — fork / app icons (`APP_ICONS`; never overwritten by sync)
- [`app/utils/icons.js`](app/utils/icons.js) — merges both (app wins on key clash) and exports `createIcon` / `initIcons`

See the **Available** lists in the template and app file headers.

## Never

- Invent, guess, or generate SVG path data (`d="…"`, `<path>`, `<svg>`, etc.)
- Paste icon markup from memory, the web, or image generation into HTML, CSS, or JS
- Duplicate SVG paths outside the icons modules above
- Add a fully drawn icon without the user providing the vector artwork

## When an icon is missing

1. **Stop** — do not substitute a made-up icon.
2. **Reuse** an existing icon if one is close enough (`data-icon`, `createIcon()`, or `{ ref: "other-icon" }`).
3. **Ask the user** to add the icon to `app/utils/icons-app.js` (forks) or `icons-template.js` (template catalogue only) — source from [Icônes — Material Icons Round](https://icones.js.org/collection/ic?s=info&variant=Round) or their own asset.
4. You may add a **blank placeholder entry** in `APP_ICONS` / `TEMPLATE_ICONS` using the template in those files (empty `markup`, correct `viewBox`) so wiring (`data-icon`, imports) can land in the same change — then tell the user to fill in the paths.

## Allowed without user-provided paths

- `data-icon="existing-id"` / `createIcon("existing-id")` for ids already in the merged `ICONS`
- `{ ref: "existing-id" }` aliases
- Blank template stub with `markup: \`\`` only when the user has agreed to add the icon

## Logo / raster assets

Brand images stay in `app/res/` — same rule: do not invent; use existing files or ask the user to supply them.
